TIP:  This is based on Ringo's version which has a different intro than Buck's.

TIP:  The intro lick also appears between the last verse and the reprise and again as the outro.  It's that step-down bomp-bomp-bomp-bomp and is pretty easy to play.  Start with all four fingers parallel to the fingerboard over frets 2 - 4.  Pick the open 3rd string (g), cover the 4th string/4th fret (f#) with your pinky and pick once, cover the 4th string/2nd fret (e) with your index finger and pick once, and pick the open 4th string (d) once followed by the chords indicated.      


